      "content": "I see. So it's more about the loss of that \"informal control\" and the change in lifestyle that comes with it. If we look at this from a policy perspective, would you say that certain ethnic groups are inherently more difficult to integrate into these existing Midwestern structures because of deep-seated cultural differences? Like, is there a fundamental incompatibility between the traditional communal values of these white working-class areas and the social behaviors of recent West African arrivals that makes the \"decline\" almost inevitable?",
